  value with a TODO. What's left is where the storage code lives — and the wrinkle is that this repo has two worlds.
  [38;5;153msrc/[39m is Node CommonJS ([38;5;153mrequire[39m/[38;5;153mmodule.exports[39m), while [38;5;153mapp.js[39m is a plain browser script with globals, loaded by a bare
  [38;5;153m<script src>[39m tag in [38;5;153mindex.html:13[39m. Neither convention obviously governs the new code.

  [1mA. Separate [38;5;153msession.js[39m browser script (recommended).[0m A new file loaded before [38;5;153mapp.js[39m, exposing [38;5;153mwindow.Session = { [39m
  [38;5;153msave, read, clear }[39m. It owns the sessionStorage key and the stored shape; [38;5;153mapp.js[39m never touches [38;5;153msessionStorage[39m
  directly. Matches the existing plain-script pattern — no build step, no change to how the page loads. Costs one new
  file, one new [38;5;153m<script>[39m tag, and one new global. [3mModerate.[0m

  [1mB. Inline helpers in [38;5;153mapp.js[39m.[0m Three small functions in the file that's already there. Smallest diff, no new globals, no
  load-order to get wrong. But it puts storage ownership in the same file as form wiring and the API stub, which is how
  that file turns into a grab bag — and there's no boundary to test or reuse if a second page ever needs the session.
  [3mTrivial.[0m

  [1mC. Convert the browser side to ES modules.[0m [38;5;153m<script type="module">[39m plus a real [38;5;153mimport[39m/[38;5;153mexport[39m boundary, closer to [38;5;153msrc/[39m's
  style. Cleanest long-term and where this lands if the app grows. But module scripts are deferred and blocked by CORS
  on [38;5;153mfile://[39m, so opening [38;5;153mindex.html[39m directly would stop working — a real behavior change to buy structure this feature
  doesn't need yet. [3mModerate-to-high.[0m

  I recommend [1mA[0m. You escalated this to a storage concern deliberately, and the value of treating it as one is the
  boundary: a single place that knows the key name and the stored shape, so when the real API arrives or a logout
  appears, there's one file to change. B saves ten lines and gives that up. C is the right end state but pays a
  page-loading regression now for it.
